# GTFO game reference

Game types used by this mod live in the r2modman profile `BepInEx\interop\` folder (`BepInEx` in `local.props`). Those DLLs are IL2CPP wrappers. `_ref/` is their type and member index. Search it before opening an interop DLL, running ILSpy, or writing another scanner.

## Where to look

- `_ref/types.tsv` — `FullName`, base type, assembly, category (`game`, `unity`, `runtime`)
- `_ref/by-assembly/<Assembly>.dll.txt` — members for that DLL
- `_ref/manifest.tsv` — profile path, sha256, counts
- `_ref/HOW.txt` — line format

Game code is mostly `Modules-ASM`, `GameData-ASM`, `Plugins-ASM`, `Addons-ASM`, `GUIX-ASM`, `SNet_ASM`. UI text is `Unity.TextMeshPro` and `UnityEngine.UI`.

Member lines: `TYPE`, `F` field, `P` property, `M` method, `E` event. Example: `rg -n "CrosshairGuiLayer" _ref/types.tsv` then open that assembly file.

## Refresh

`_ref/` is generated and gitignored. From the repo root, when `manifest.tsv` is missing or the game/profile interop changed:

```powershell
dotnet run --project tools/DumpGameRef -c Release
```

Matching sha256 values skip the rebuild. `--force` rebuilds anyway. Keep the dump local.

One-off wrapper source goes in `_ref/decompiled/<Type>.cs`. Read that file on the next lookup.
